reset all
panel set Bench

silent=t
spec back
txt font 4
txt centre
txt colour orange
txt c -20 "How to allow the use of the accumulation buffer"

txt lineskip 24
txt c a " "
txt left
txt colour white


txt 30 a "The `accumulation buffer' is a very nice feature in OpenGL that allows for"
txt 30 a "numerous interesting visual effects, for example motion blur."
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "Unfortunately, some graphics cards give very poor performance or even"
txt 30 a "incorrect results when using the accumulation buffer.  Since several"
txt 30 a "KnotPlot demos use the accumulation buffer for a motion blur effect, it's"
txt 30 a "important to make sure that your accumulation buffer is working properly"
txt 30 a "before allowing its use."
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "Here is what you do:"
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "   --- click on the `accbuff' buttons in the `Other graphics tests'"
txt 30 a "       section on the control panel"
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "   --- compare your results to the reference renderings on the web"
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "   --- if performance is reasonable (frame rate is pretty good) AND you"
txt 30 a "       get the correct rendering (or close enough), then click on the"
txt 30 a "             `allow accbuff permanently'"
txt 30 a "       button you see on the control panel.  This will enable the"
txt 30 a "       accumulation buffer in all future KnotPlot sessions."
txt 30 a " "
txt 30 a "   --- you can also disallow accumulation buffer use permanently (next button)"
txt 30 a "       in case you find you don't want the accumulation buffer to be used"
txt 30 a " "

txt font 3
txt centre
txt lineskip 14
txt c a "Rob Scharein"
txt c a "17 April 2007"

silent=f
txt on

